title: what is mine, and where my neighbours begin
pid: df60c797-bd12-4bac-a137-e15a4fbb5e90
body: |2-
  Mine: 'server/refresh/' (but 'refresh/diff_view.rs'), 'server/rerender_pass.rs',
  'server/update_buffer.rs', 'server/org_to_text.rs', 'server/view_text_delta.rs' (the
  redraw delta), 'server/heralds.rs', 'server/herald_tokens.rs', 'server/body_view_escape.rs',
  'server/types/viewnode.rs', 'server/types/views_state.rs', 'server/serve/rerender_stream.rs',
  and the handlers 'single_root_view.rs', 'rerender_views.rs', 'rerender_all_views.rs', 'herald_rules.rs'.
  [[id:d2541653-2df0-4b97-ba7b-3297558f12bc][Jesus]] (saving) hands me the swapped-in graph at 'update_views_after_save'.
  [[id:193e5740-ecd9-45df-ac13-e1b0b17ceecc][Vic]] (version control and the diff view) owns 'server/graph_straddle/' and
  'server/diff_view/', whose 'buffer_rerender.rs' calls my refresh. The override rules of
  [[id:deb5f0e5-6abe-436e-85bd-d9e7d0d41238][Sue]] (subscriptions, forks, overrides, hides) shape 'refresh/id_rule.rs' and the
  substitution steps of 'refresh/visit.rs'. [[id:c1c373a8-06a5-4b13-9379-8e3eaed8efa3][Elle]] (the Emacs client) shows what I
  send: the text, the redraw delta and the herald facts are my contract, her overlays
  and buffer handling are hers. What a restricted viewnode may show is [[id:9327f310-8082-4e42-91b4-f116ccac24ce][Praveen]] (privacy)'s.
